{0 Server-side programming}

Eliom can be used as a traditional server-side Web framework, where the
server generates the pages. These chapters are also the basis of
client-server applications.

- {{!//server/services/page-index}Services} are the entry points of a Web
  site: how to create them, type their parameters, write their handlers, and
  link to them.
- {{!//server/page-state}Sessions and server side state}: Eliom references
  keep data on the server for one user, one client process or a group of
  sessions, in memory or on disk.
- {{!//server/page-security}Security}: what Eliom and Ocsigen Server take
  care of, and what is left to the programmer.
- {{!//server/page-widgets}HTML widgets}: images, style sheets, scripts and
  menus.
